<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n19659" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">βᾰΰζω</span></b>  (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">βαύζω</span>
		disyll. <i><span class="en">
			Lyc.
			1453
		</span></i> is <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				f.l. for
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">βάζω</span>
			), 
				Dor.
			
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">βαΰσδω</span></b> , onomatop. word,
				<i>cry</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">βαύ βαύ,</span>
			<i>bark,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Theoc.
				6.10
			</span></i>; of angry persons, <i>snarl, yelp,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">παῦσαι βαΰζων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ar.
					<u>Th.</u>
					173
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				805
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τάδε σῖγά τις βαΰζει</span>
			thus they <i>snarl</i> in secret, <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Ag.</u>
				449
			</span></i> (lyr.); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἷ᾽ ἄττα β.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Cratin.
					6
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> trans.,
				<i>shriek aloud for,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τινά</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Pers.</u>
					13
				</span></i>
			; of dogs, <i>bark at,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τινά</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Heraclit.
					97
				</span></i>
			 codd.</div>
